Unreleased - Phil Randal, Claude
    Fix the unexpected-argument check: it never fired

2026-11-25 - Phil Randal, DeepSeek and Claude - Release 1.42
    A Rust port of gpsctl now exists: https://github.com/philrandal/gpsctl-rs (it follows release 1.42 of this program).
        README.md points to it.
    Removed the commented-out PPS signal test (--test) and its wiringPi references: wiringPi is deprecated and the option was already disabled
    CFG-NAV5 integer bounds (min elevation ±90, fix mode 1–3, dynamic model 0/2–10, Bike=10, excludes 11–13)
    getConfigUTCStandard() accepts {0,3,5,6,7,8,9}; EU/NPLI/NICT names; local enum in ublox.c
        (the check itself was missing from the code until now: anything else is reported and the default, USNO, used)
    Quiet mode reports the real failure cause instead of "Errors occurred!"; option errors say invalid option "--bogus"
    When querying configuration, NMEA version 4.11 is now displayed correctly as 4.11 in both text and JSON outputs (it
        previously printed as 4.b in text and 5.1 in JSON due to 0x4B hex encoding).
    safeMalloc() safely handles size 0 requests without failing on platforms where malloc(0) returns NULL, and qsort()
        is guarded against zero-satellite queries.
    The gpsctl:sync method configuration option now requires at least syncASCII (1), preventing syncNone (0) from being
        accepted and failing during autobaud/sync.
    Plugged several memory leaks: freed slReturn records in sendUbxAckedMsg(), autoBaudRate(), and actionAutoBaud(); cleared
        dangling abResp pointer in actionAutoBaud(); and freed the iniparser dictionary before program exit.
    waitForQuietLine() stops with "serial port hung up" when read() returns zero (it used to spin on a hung-up port for up to
        a second).  After a hardware restart that gets no answer, the error now suggests the -a option (the receiver may
        have come back at its saved baud rate), and the factory reset sets the client's baud rate from the one constant.
    The NMEA version setting is checked against the versions u-blox defines (2.1, 2.3, 4.0, 4.1 or 4.10, 4.11; or the
        digits 21, 23, 40, 41, 410, 411): anything else is reported and the default (4.1) used.  4.11 is now sent as 0x4B (it
        used to be sent as 0x41, i.e. 4.1).  Decimal settings (fixed altitude and its variance, DoP masks) are range-checked
        against the size of the field they go in, and the scaling no longer overflows an int.
    --save_config help text and README now say what is saved where: battery-backed RAM, and flash, EEPROM and SPI flash if
        the module has them (the save has used device mask 0x17 since 1.40).
    GPSCTL_TRACE=1 in the environment prints every byte sent to and received from the serial port (received bytes grouped
        32 to a line), with receive-buffer flushes, host baud changes and quiet-line waits, and times, to stderr.
    Autobaud (UBX sync method) now listens before it polls.  Every poll sent at a wrong baud rate is a burst of frame
        errors in the receiver, and a u-blox that sees more than 100 switches its UART receiver off ("UART RX was
        disabled") for a few minutes - deaf even at the right rate, so autobaud failed outright.  The first pass now
        sends nothing, listening at each rate (1.5 s) for the receiver's own NMEA; only the rate where valid NMEA is
        heard gets a UBX poll.  A receiver with NMEA off falls back to the old poll-at-every-rate pass, which now
        starts at most two polls per rate (it used to start a third that couldn't finish).
    After the host's baud rate changes (autobaud, -b, --factory_reset), discard input until the line has been quiet for 20 ms
        (at most 1 s) before the first command.  A UART can't find character boundaries while a busy receiver keeps
        sending (the u-blox defaults nearly fill a 9600 baud line), so the reply to a poll sent at once came back with its
        B5 sync byte corrupted, and autobaud could fail on the right rate.

2026-11-22 - Phil Randal, DeepSeek, and Claude - Release 1.41
    New option --factory_reset=yes: restores the receiver's factory defaults 
        (CFG-CFG clearing and loading all sections, so the saved configuration
        is erased too), follows the receiver back to its default 9600 baud, then 
        restarts it (hot-start hardware reset).  The word yes is required, so the
        option can't be given by accident.
    More fixes in ublox.c

2026-11-22 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.40
    GNSS change: UBX-CFG-GNSS is sent only if it changes something (each one makes the receiver 
        restart its GNSS engine).
    After a CFG-GNSS, wait 0.5 s before the next command, as u-blox requires.
    If Galileo is enabled, the GNSS change is followed by what u-blox requires: 
        save the configuration (CFG-CFG, 0x041B, so that the reset does not discard 
        it), a hardware reset (CFG-RST, hot start), then wait for the receiver to answer again.

2026-11-20 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.39
    Oversized UBX length: treated as noise instead of waiting for up to 65535 bytes.
    Synchronizer wait: longer wait in the autobaud sync at slow baud rates.
    Poll and ACK waits: the same extra allowance for every poll and ACK wait.
    Config values: strict decimal reading, with the units in the shipped configs moved into comments.
      NOTE: this breaks existing configs - please adjust your gpsctl.conf to put comment symbols 
          after numeric values

2026-11-20 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.38
    Refuse a shared serial port and cross-check autobaud

