2026-11-16 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.35
    sl_options: compare unsigned with unsigned in addOptionRecord
    Pass unsigned char values to the ctype functions
    sl_options: drop the impossible maxCount < 0 check
    sl_options: fix memory leaks in the help output and warning results
    sl_general: make sleep_ns sleep for a second or more, and through signals
    sl_serial: set VMIN and VTIME in setTermOptions
    gpsctl: stop the --query option definition shadowing the queryDef type
    gpsctl: make cmpSatellite static and const-correct
    gpsctl: reject empty and out-of-range integer arguments
    gpsctl: treat an empty yes/no argument as no, and document 'on'
    gpsctl: flush echoed NMEA output a line at a time
    ublox: only change the UART1 rate in ubxEnableNMEAMsg
    ublox: don't truncate the CFG-GNSS block limit to 8 bits
    ublox: only apply the NAV-PVT time correction to a valid time
    ublox: resync after a bad UBX frame instead of failing on it
    ublox: validate CFG-NMEA reply size in ubxConfigNMEAVersion
    ublox: round scaled NAV5 config values instead of truncating

2026-11-15 - Phil Randal and OpenCode / DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free - Release 1.34
    Fix auto-baudrate detection logic

2026-11-15 - Phil Randal and OpenCode / DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free - Release 1.33
    Wait for every byte of a message to be sent, rather than giving up on a partial write.
    Report a hung-up serial port as such, rather than as a failure to write.
    Check the size of each configuration reply before using it, so a short reply is reported
        rather than decoded as a zeroed configuration.
    Reopen the port during recovery only when it really works again, not merely when it opens.
    Fix a memory leak when an option name is generated.
    Widen the PRr column in the satellite table, which a negative residual pushed out of line.
    Run gpsctl up to three times at boot, 15 seconds apart, and log the errors.

2026-11-15 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.31
    Add retry if serial port fails
    Another memory leak patched

