    More sync error fixes

2026-11-13 - Phil Randal and OpenCode / DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free - Release 1.29
    Better fix for sync errors

2026-11-13 - Phil Randal and Claude - Release 1.28
    Make --help, --version and -U work without a serial port. 
       They now exit 0 on a machine with no /dev/serial0. Before, they exited 1.
    Fix frame sync when a stray B5 comes right before a real frame (B5 B5 62 …).
        That frame is now received; before, it was dropped.
    Zero-fill new buffers in create_slBuffer, so no uninitialised bytes get through.
    Do the currentTimeMs arithmetic in 64 bits. Affects 32-bit architectures only.
    Clear the stale checksum tail when a new $ starts.
        Before, a bad-checksum line followed by an empty line could report the NMEA
        synchronizer as locked. Valid sentences still lock.
    Check the NAV-SAT body size and clamps the satellite count to what the message actually holds.
        A body shorter than 8 bytes is now rejected. Before, a claimed count of 200 with 2 
        satellites present was accepted.
    Fix minor error message bugs.
    Retry a timed-out UBX sync twice, so three attempts in all.

